{"author_id": "22346932", "conversation_id": "2099900501680701530", "created_at": "2026-09-15T19:23:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2099942130470809814"], "id": "2099942130470809814", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 102, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2099939747086946515", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@thorcmd Interesting question. It could be Jews, Arabs (20% of Israelis), Palestinians\u2026 depends a lot on how Denmark manages its stats. I\u2019m not close enough to them to tell.", "username": "tomaspueyo", "author_followers": 332526}
{"author_id": "22346932", "conversation_id": "2099900501680701530", "created_at": "2026-09-15T19:24:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2099942473296441781"], "id": "2099942473296441781", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1837, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2099935548626391133", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@markessien Across 5 countries in Europe, these are tens of thousands, or hundreds of thousands. This is not a sample size error. More importantly, all the data points in the same direction.", "username": "tomaspueyo", "author_followers": 332526}
{"author_id": "22346932", "conversation_id": "2099900501680701530", "created_at": "2026-09-15T19:26:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2099942841891819989"], "id": "2099942841891819989", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 9632, "like_count": 103, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2099928254807151008", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Otvadzaglaviata That\u2019s crazy. It reminds me of how in some country Kuwait stands for Palestinians, and that\u2019s why Kuwaitis are at the top", "username": "tomaspueyo", "author_followers": 332526}
